  "worked_solution": "We consider the augmented matrix $[B\\,|\\,I]$ where $I$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix. Applying the indicated row operations we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  \\\\  & =[I\\,|\\,{B}^{-1}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse matrix is \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
